message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Ceuta Me Preocupa: a privacy-preserving citizen mailbox with AI-assisted de-identification and classification"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Peral Sánchez"
    given-names: "David Jesús"
    affiliation: "Cátedra Ceuta-IATEB, Universidad de Granada"
  - family-names: "Romero Olmedo"
    given-names: "Adrián"
    affiliation: "Cátedra Ceuta-IATEB, Universidad de Granada"
repository-code: "https://github.com/David0450/ceuta-me-preocupa"
url: "https://ceutamepreocupa.es/buzon"
doi: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24082092"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Ceuta Me Preocupa is a virtual citizen mailbox for the Autonomous City of
  Ceuta (Spain). A Laravel web application collects concerns and improvement
  proposals, keeps personal data apart from the working record and gives
  authorised reviewers a panel to confirm, correct and route each submission
  to the competent public body. A Python pipeline running a locally hosted
  large language model (Qwen3-8B) proposes a de-identified text, a category,
  subcategories and an urgency level, which are always checked by a human
  reviewer.
version: "2.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
keywords:
  - citizen participation
  - e-government
  - de-identification
  - text classification
  - large language models
